RegEx is a pattern-matching language used for string validation and manipulation.”

2. Why RegEx in Java?
Input validation (email, phone, password)
Search & replace
Data extraction (logs, files)
Request validation in Spring Boot

3. RegEx Support in Java (Core Classes)
Java provides RegEx via java.util.regex package
| Class                    | Purpose                    |
| ------------------------ | -------------------------- |
| `Pattern`                | Compiled regex             |
| `Matcher`                | Matches pattern with input |
| `PatternSyntaxException` | Invalid regex              |

4. Basic Flow (🔥 MUST KNOW)
Pattern p = Pattern.compile("regex");
Matcher m = p.matcher("input");
while (m.find()) {
    System.out.println(m.group());
}

5. Simple RegEx Example
import java.util.regex.*;
public class Test {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Pattern p = Pattern.compile("Java");
        Matcher m = p.matcher("Java is Java");

        while (m.find()) {
            System.out.println(m.group());
        }
    }
}

Output
Java
Java

